  "status": "completed",
  "output": "The edit went wrong — the `Edit` tool interpreted `$'\\n'` as a newline in the replacement, so the file got mangled. Fixing it now with a byte-exact rewrite of just that line.Done. Line 3 is now `IFS=$'\\n'` and every other line is unchanged.\n\nOne thing worth knowing: `read` only reads a single line, so with newline splitting the script now emits only the first field — `./split_lines.sh $'a\\nb\\nc'` prints `[a]`. To split a multi-line argument you'd need something like `mapfile -t parts <<< \"$1\"` instead of `read`. I left that alone since you asked for only the one-line change.",
